 !!! Warning
     The `tradable_balance_ratio` setting applies to the current balance (free balance + tied up in trades). Therefore, assuming the starting balance of 1000, a configuration with `tradable_balance_ratio=0.99` will not guarantee that 10 currency units will always remain available on the exchange. For example, the free amount may reduce to 5 units if the total balance is reduced to 500 (either by a losing streak or by withdrawing balance).
 
+#### Currency exposure limit
+
+If several of your pairs are priced against, or margined in, the same underlying (quote) currency - for example several pairs quoted in the same stablecoin, or several BTC-margined futures - a move in that one currency can hit all of those trades at once. `max_currency_exposure` limits what share of your tradable capital may be committed at once to open trades sharing the same underlying currency, regardless of how many individual pairs that spans.
+
+For example, with `max_currency_exposure=0.5`, no more than 50% of your tradable capital can be committed at any one time to trades whose pair is quoted in the same currency - even if each individual trade's stake size looks fine on its own. When opening (or adding to, via [position adjustment](strategy-callbacks.md#adjust-trade-position)) a trade would push the combined exposure to that currency above the limit, the stake amount is reduced to fit under it - the same way stake amounts are already reduced to fit exchange or balance limits - or the trade is skipped entirely if no room is left. This is enforced identically in live/dry-run and in backtesting.
+
+This defaults to `1.0` (100%), which disables the limit.
+
 #### Assign available Capital
 
 To fully utilize compounding profits when using multiple bots on the same exchange account, you'll want to limit each bot to a certain starting balance.
